            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "- For Row-based data sources",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontSize": "11pt"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": ": By default, the Power KPI Matrix visual will display various metrics ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "alphabetically, ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontStyle": "italic",
                      "fontSize": "11pt"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "according to the Actual Value metric name.  ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "- For Column-based data sources",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontSize": "11pt"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": ": By default, Power KPI Matrix will display various metrics in the same order the columns were originally dropped on to the Actual Value bucket. This can be changed to alphabetic order by going into the Default Sort Order dropdown of the Table section in the Format Pane.  Keep in mind, if you stay with the default behavior and later change your mind on the order of an individual metric, you will need to remove the fields from Actual Value and re-add in the desired order.  If you have many different metrics and better control over order, consider explicitly defining your custom sort order (below).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Custom Sort Order of Metrics",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "textDecoration": "underline"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "In the Field Pane, a ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "Sort Order ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontSize": "11pt"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "bucket is available for custom sorting of metrics. The Sort Order bucket requires a simple table that lists the unique metric names along with a column that specifies the desired sequence number.  Here are the setup steps to enable custom sorting.  Note that many of the steps overlap with those of using Hyperlinks and Categories, so if you are already using those features, you may skip some of these steps, as indicated.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Setup Steps:",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "1. Add a Table of Metric Names ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "color": "#000000"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "(see \"_Links\" table examples)",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "color": "#000000"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "2. Perform Final Configuration",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "color": "#000000"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "1. Add a Table of Metric Names:",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "textDecoration": "underline"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "To accomplish this, you must include a table with a column that includes the ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "color": "#000000"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "exact",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "textDecoration": "underline",
                      "color": "#000000"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": " [metric name] [type=text] you wish to link and another column with the [target url].  In this sample file, there are two identical tables, Col_Links and Row_Links.  Both tables are provided because one is used for the default column-based data model approach while the other is used to illustrate joining to a table with row-based metric names.  ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "color": "#000000"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "For Column-based data only: ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "color": "#000000"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "Add an ID column (whole number type) to both your data (fact) table and your [links] lookup table. Populate the rows of the ID column in the [links] table with unique numbers, starting with number 1.  In the fact table, you need to add the same numbers for the first ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "color": "#000000"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "n",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontStyle": "italic",
                      "color": "#000000"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": " rows, where ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "color": "#000000"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "n",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontStyle": "italic",
                      "color": "#000000"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": " is the max number of rows in your links table. Optionally, repeat the number series for the rest of your rows in your fact table (this is necessary if you are going to filter the visual based on date). See the sample tables in this file",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "color": "#000000"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
